# Go
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# Go workspaces. Never committed, deliberately: a go.work puts every workspace
# module into a single build list, so the cloud SDKs required by the modules
# under modules/ would take part in version selection for the root module too,
# and `bin/nexus` built on a contributor's machine could resolve different
# transitive versions than the binary CI and the release build. Keeping the root
# module's dependency graph exactly what go.mod says is the whole reason those
# backends live in separate modules. Each submodule carries a `replace` pointing
# at ../.. instead, which is scoped to that module and affects nothing else.
# A local go.work for an editor is fine -- that is why these are ignored rather
# than merely absent. See docs/src/guides/go-modules.md.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Docs
docs/book/

# Eval harness — generated reports (cases/ is source and stays tracked)
tests/eval/reports/

